# Continuation power flow

This branch follows a network through increasing load, past the point where the ordinary power flow fails, and finds the nose of the voltage curve.

## Choosing A Surface

Use `trace` for the voltage at a load that may be close to collapse and, with `TraceStop::Nose`, for the loading margin.

## Practical Examples

The examples exercise the principal surface of this branch.

### Example 1

A line against its closed-form nose.

@@example Eng/api/power_trace_nose.cpp@@

### Example 2

